==============================================================================
Data corpora (RAG)
==============================================================================

The RAG knowledge bases include the nine OHADA Uniform Acts (3,126 articles),
sourced from the HuggingFace dataset "Maathis-com/ohada-actes-uniformes",
licensed under CC-BY-4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
The AUDCIF (accounting law) is routed to the `rag_erp` schema; the eight other
acts to `rag_legal`.

Modifications: routed per act, reformatted per article, chunked and embedded for
retrieval. See scripts/ingest_ohada.py and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

The cyber knowledge base (`rag_cyber`) combines international security standards
with Congolese law:
  - NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0 and SP 800-53r5 / 800-61r3 / 800-171r3 —
    U.S. Government works, public domain (17 U.S.C. §105).
  - OWASP Top 10 (2021), Application Security Verification Standard 5.0, and
    Cheat Sheet Series — (C) OWASP Foundation, licensed CC-BY-SA 4.0
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), extracted from the OWASP
    GitHub repositories.
  - MITRE ATT&CK(R) Enterprise (defensive subset: descriptions, detections,
    mitigations) — (C) The MITRE Corporation, used under the ATT&CK Terms of Use;
    the underlying STIX data is Apache-2.0. ATT&CK is a registered trademark of
    The MITRE Corporation.
  - Congolese laws n°29-2019 (data protection), n°26-2020 (cybersecurity),
    n°27-2020 (cybercrime), n°30-2019 (ANSSI-Congo) — official public texts.

Modifications: fetched, OCR'd (Congolese laws) or extracted from markdown/STIX
(OWASP/MITRE), cleaned, chunked and embedded. See scripts/extract_owasp.py,
scripts/extract_mitre_attack.py, scripts/ocr_scan.py and ingest_manifest.yml.
The ANSSI guides are NOT included (unresolved commercial-license conflict);
ISO 27001/27002 and CIS Controls/Benchmarks are not included either.
